# The interpreter Dependabot takes for requirements.txt beside this file.
# It reads a .python-version in the directory it scans ahead of the
# root's, and the root's names the newest interpreter the test matrix
# covers, which Dependabot can be yet to support: the Dependency Graph's
# pip job for this directory then fails, and the packages requirements.txt
# pins go without Dependabot alerts.
#
# 3.11 is the interpreter that installs requirements.txt: PYTHON_VERSION
# in the config of the image the Dockerfile's digest names. Nothing keeps
# the two in step. An image of another minor version leaves requirements.txt
# resolved here under an interpreter the image no longer installs it with;
# a Dependabot that no longer supports 3.11 fails the pip job here as the
# root's pin does. Dependabot matches the major and minor version alone,
# so no patch is written here.
#
# uv reads this file too, for a command run in this directory, so a
# whole-line comment only, for the reason the root .python-version gives.
3.11
